>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `del_split`

``` hol4
simpLib.del_split : string -> simpset -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removes split rules from a simpset.

`del_split name ss` removes the loopers `split name` and
`split_asm name` added by `add_split`; if `name` itself begins with
`split ` or `split_asm `, only that looper is removed. Rules with the
`split` attribute are unaffected; disable them for one call with
`ExclX ("split:" ^ name)`; see [`simpLib.ExclX`](#simpLib.ExclX).
To retract an attribute rule persistently for descendant replay, use
`splitLib.exclude_split "Thy.Name"` after explicit registration.
Local `del_split` never needs persistent registration.

### Failure

Never fails. Returns `ss` if no such looper exists.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val c = Context.snapshot();
>>_ val opt_ss = simpLib.add_split (splitLib.type_split_of “:'a option”)
                   bool_ss;
>> SIMP_TAC (simpLib.del_split "option$option_CASE" opt_ss) []
     ([], “P (case x of NONE => 0 | SOME n => n + 1) : bool”) c;
```

### See also

[`splitLib.exclude_split`](#splitLib.exclude_split),
[`simpLib.add_split`](#simpLib.add_split),
[`simpLib.split_ss`](#simpLib.split_ss).
